-- The default summary instructions are now a short news paragraph. Monitors still on the previous default move to it.
.bail on
UPDATE monitor SET summary_prompt = 'Write 2 to 4 sentences as one flowing paragraph, like a short news item, not a report. No bullet points, headings or labelled sections, even as plain text: don''t write "Topic: detail" one per line or sentence (for example "Infrastructure: council approved X. Housing: council discussed Y."), which is a list dressed up as prose. Write it the way you''d describe the meeting to someone out loud, with one topic flowing into the next. Focus on the most significant decisions and discussions.'
  WHERE summary_prompt IN ('Write for a resident who didn''t attend. Plain language, no jargon, no filler. Lead with what matters most: decisions, money, land use and anything a resident could speak to. Use short paragraphs or a few bullet points, under 250 words. Name the item numbers or bylaw numbers people would search for, and say what''s being decided, not just the title.', 'Write for a resident who didn''t attend. Plain language, no jargon, no filler. Lead with what matters most: decisions, money, land use and anything a resident could speak to. Use short paragraphs or a few bullet points. Name the item numbers or bylaw numbers people would search for, and say what''s being decided, not just the title.');
